  {
   "index": 18,
   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 634,
   "text": "She went on to compete for Sydney FC and Canberra United and had a stint in Portugal. Long before making her W-League debut at 19, football was already part of her life. Her parents took her to her dad’s games as a newborn, and she spent weekends on the sidelines watching him play. Her grandparents in Mount Morgan had also founded the first football club in their small country town.\nNow, Allira is",
